claim.claim-text:
a cap having at least a first aperture and a second aperture extending therethrough;
a first flexible member extendable from, and retractable inwardly of, the first aperture in the cap, the first flexible member having a distal end coupled to a first bendable coupling;
a first arm extending from the first bendable coupling, the first arm pivotable, with respect to the distal end of the first flexible member, through the first bendable coupling, and a second arm connected to the first arm through a second bendable coupling and pivotable, with respect to the first arm, through the second bendable coupling;
a second flexible member extendable from, and retractable inwardly of, the second aperture in the cap, the second flexible member having a distal end coupled to a third bendable coupling;
a third arm extending from the second bendable coupling, the third arm pivotable, with respect to the distal end of the second flexible member, through the third bendable coupling, and a fourth arm connected to the third arm through a fourth bendable coupling and pivotable, with respect to the third arm, through the fourth bendable coupling;
a first end effector connected to the second arm; and
a second end effector operatively connected to the fourth arm.

extending a first flexible member, having a distal end coupled to a first bendable coupling, inwardly of the sheath;
providing a first arm extending from the first bendable coupling, the first arm pivotable, with respect to the distal end of the first flexible member, through the first bendable coupling, and a second arm connected to the first arm through a second bendable coupling and pivotable, with respect to the first arm, through the second bendable coupling;
extending a second flexible member, having a distal end coupled to a third bendable coupling, inwardly of the sheath;
providing third arm extending from the third bendable coupling, the third arm pivotable, with respect to the distal end of the second flexible member, through the third bendable coupling, and a fourth arm connected to the third arm through a fourth bendable coupling and pivotable, with respect to the third arm, through the fourth bendable coupling;
providing a first end effector connected to the second arm;
extending the first arm, the second arm, and the first end effector outwardly of the cap;
pivoting the first arm with respect to the first flexible member through the first bendable coupling; and
pivoting the second arm with respect to the first arm through the second bendable coupling.
